 "notes": [
  "Total 60 as published. The strategy says 'ALWAYS START WITH DS' (Death Star system) with Oppressive Enforcement in most matchups; against Mind What You Have Learned (and optionally vs Hidden Base or Ewok drain) it starts Hoth: Defensive Perimeter instead. No Objective.",
  "Battle Order, Secret Plans, Oppressive Enforcement, Come Here You Big Coward and There Is No Try are the pre-Reflections III Effects, not Defensive Shields.",
  "Posted 'Defensive Perimeter' dested Hoth: Defensive Perimeter (3rd Marker); 'Hoth Ice Plain' Hoth: Ice Plains (5th Marker); 'Hoth Docking Bay' Hoth: Echo Docking Bay (Dark); 'U-3P0' U-3PO (Yoo-Threepio); 'Dreadnaught' Dreadnaught-Class Heavy Cruiser; 'Vader's Personnal Shuttle' Vader's Personal Shuttle; 'Those Rebel Won't Escape Us' Those Rebels Won't Escape Us; 'Oppresive Enforcement' Oppressive Enforcement.",
  "The title marks this as a revision of the author's earlier 'Hard Toulouse' post. The strategy says it was used at 'my regional' and a team tournament the next day (lost only 1 game, to HBX); the events are not named, so the deck is filed as general."
